{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event type names the purpose it is collected for, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", which is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unless the type says otherwise. Give the tracker a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"type":"text","text":", which the app updates as the user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decides, and an event reaches a destination only once its category is granted:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct AdClicked: Event {","    static let consentCategory = ConsentCategory.advertising","    var campaign: String","}","","let consent = Consent([.analytics: .granted])","let tracker = Tracker(consent: consent)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: ConsoleDestination(),","    ConsoleDestination().accepting(.advertising)",")","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))          \/\/ delivered: analytics is granted","tracker.track(AdClicked(campaign: \"spring\"))  \/\/ held: advertising is undecided","consent.grant(.advertising)                   \/\/ delivers the held AdClicked"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracker given no consent delivers every event."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Undecided-granted-and-denied","type":"heading","text":"Undecided, granted and denied"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A category is undecided until the app grants or denies it. While it is undecided, its events are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held in memory, not written to a store, up to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"heldRecordLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" records (1,000 by default) across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every category, the oldest dropped first when the hold is full. Granting delivers them in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were tracked, before anything tracked after the grant. Denying drops them. Events tracked while"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their category is denied are never collected."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"grant","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" return at once: they record the decision, and the tracker’s worker releases or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops what it held. Every drop of a record that was held or kept is reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"consent.dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ConsentDropReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as it happens, so none is lost silently. Held","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records are lost if the app ends first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Records that a store recovered from an earlier run are gated again as the tracker starts. They are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held outside the bound, since the store still keeps them, and the store forgets each one that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"denied.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Destinations","type":"heading","text":"Destinations"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A destination receives every category the consent lets through, unless ","type":"text"},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" narrows it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the categories it serves, as the second destination above takes only advertising.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article","title":"Consent Gating"},"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending."}],"title":"Persisting Records","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","abstract":[{"text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen.","type":"text"}],"title":"Automatic Tracking","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","title":"Defining Events","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","title":"Sampling Events","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it."}],"title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"title":"Sessions and Standard Context","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"title":"Traffluent","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"}}}